For the first time since Apple started selling standard and "Pro" iPhones, we're not going to get an entry-level iPhone model this fall. Apple doesn't plan to release an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18/">iPhone 18</a> in September, and will only launch the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a>, &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max, and foldable <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/iphone-ultra/">iPhone Ultra</a>. The lower-cost &zwnj;iPhone 18&zwnj; won't come out until spring 2027.<br/>
<br/>
